        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most DIYers coating a dry basement, shop or garage slab, Rust-Oleum EpoxyShield Professional is the practical pick. RockSolid is the faster-turnaround choice, and Leggari's polyaspartic gives the most durable DIY floor to anyone who can grind and work quickly. ArmorPoxy fits heavy-use shops, Granite Grip fits patios and other outdoor foot-traffic slabs, and Siloxa-Tek 8500 protects concrete with no coating at all.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, the slab underneath sets the ceiling. Check for sealers and moisture, grind or etch to the profile the maker specifies, mix only what you can spread, and let every layer cure fully. Get those steps right and a coated concrete floor can look sharp and stay bonded for a decade.
